1. LLM with long context window: take `tender` as an input, divide it by logical sections (pages from - to `json sections`) 

output example:

```json
{
    "number_of_sections": 3,
    "sections" :
    [
        {
            "num": 1,
            "page_from": 1,
            "page_to": 18, 
            "desc": "ai description of section 1",
        },
        {
            "num": 2,
            "page_from": 18,
            "page_to": 25, 
            "desc": "ai description of section 2",
        },
        {
            "num": 3,
            "page_from": 25,
            "page_to": 40, 
            "desc": "ai description of section 2",
        }
    ]
}
```

2. (script?) Input (pdf) is cut into different sections; input: `tender`, `json sections`; output: `tender_<num_x>.pdf`

3. Each section is feed into parallel <agent> which write `lv position` for the section;
input: `tender_<num_x>.pdf` into `llm`; output: `tender_lv_positions_<num_x>.csv` (for each <agent> should be <comparator agent> which verify each newly created position in `tender_lv_positions_<num_x>.csv` if it actually exist in `input`);

4. (script?) Merge `tender_lv_positions_<num_x>.csv` into `tender_lv_positions.csv` (`like in materials/example_lv_positions.csv`)

5. Match `tender_lv_positions.csv` and validate existence each of item in `materials/catalog.csv` and create `tender_lv_ouput.json` (similar to `materials/expected_output_example.json`)

*Compare descriptions, dimensions and manufacturers.

part of json output example

```json

    {
      "lv_id": "LV0006",
      "source_page": 80,
      "matched_product_id": "P-SIL-001",
      "install_code": "SILENCER",
      "quantity": 4.0,
      "unit": "pc",
      "net_unit_cost_chf": 2600.0,
      "material_cost_chf": 10816.0,
      "adjusted_install_hours": 11.24,
      "labour_cost_chf": 1078.56,
      "direct_position_cost_chf": 11894.56,
      "price_source": "supplier_package",
      "match_confidence": 0.72,
      "review_required": true,
      "status": "supplier_quote_required"
    },

```
